Let $C$ be the temperature of the water.
Let $T$ be the time Rey takes to swim a mile of distance.
When the water is cold, Rey swims 1 mile in 16 minutes.
So, $T_C = 16$ minutes per mile.
When the water is warm, Rey swims a mile in 2 minutes more than twice as long as before.
Let $T_W$ be the time Rey takes to swim a mile of warm water.
$T_W = 2T_C + 2$ minutes per mile.
$T_W = 2(16) + 2 = 32 + 2 = 34$ minutes per mile.
We need to find how much longer Rey takes to swim 3 miles on a hot day than on a cold day.
Time taken to swim 3 miles on a cold day is $3 \times T_C = 3 \times 16 = 48$ minutes.
Time taken to swim 3 miles on a hot day is $3 \times T_W = 3 \times 34 = 102$ minutes.
The difference in time is $102 - 48 = 54$ minutes.

